<section class="hero"><div class="breadcrumb"><a href="index.html">Associate</a><span class="sep">›</span><a href="#">Module 8</a><span class="sep">›</span><span>Output Formatting</span></div><span class="hero-eyebrow">Module 8 · Lesson 4</span><h1>Output Formatting and Structured Responses</h1><p class="hero-sub">Learn how to request specific output formats from LLMs and parse structured responses. Master JSON formatting, lists, tables, and custom templates. Understand how to guide models toward predictable, machine-readable outputs that integrate seamlessly with downstream applications and automation workflows.</p></section>

<div class="objectives"><h4>Learning Objectives</h4><ul><li>Request JSON output and parse responses programmatically with the OpenAI API</li><li>Use schema-based prompting for consistent, structured data extraction</li><li>Extract tables, lists, and nested objects in predictable formats</li><li>Implement robust output validation and error handling for malformed responses</li><li>Integrate structured responses with Python applications and databases</li><li>Handle edge cases and gracefully manage parsing failures in production systems</li></ul></div>

<section class="section" id="json-fundamentals"><span class="section-label">Fundamentals</span><h2>JSON Output Formatting</h2><p>JSON (JavaScript Object Notation) is the industry standard for machine-readable structured data. When you ask an LLM to return JSON, you get predictable outputs that your code can parse directly into Python dictionaries and work with programmatically. This is critical when building production systems that need reliable data extraction.</p>

<p>The key to successful JSON extraction is being explicit and unambiguous in your requests. Tell the model to return ONLY valid JSON, specify exactly what keys you need, and ideally show an example of the format you want.</p>

<div class="code-header"><span class="code-lang">Python</span><button class="copy-btn">Copy</button></div><pre><code><span class="kw">from</span> <span class="im">openai</span> <span class="kw">import</span> <span class="fn">OpenAI</span>
<span class="kw">import</span> <span class="im">json</span>

<span class="va">client</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">OpenAI</span>()

<span class="cm"># Request JSON response explicitly with clear instructions</span>
<span class="va">prompt</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="st">"""Extract key information about this product and return ONLY valid JSON.
Product: Premium wireless headphones with noise cancellation
Price: $199.99
Categories: Electronics, Audio Equipment, Wireless Devices

Return valid JSON with exactly these keys:
- name (string)
- price (number, without currency symbol)
- categories (array of strings)
- features (array of strings, make up 2-3 realistic features)
- rating (number 1-5 scale)

Example format:
{"name":"...", "price":0, "categories":[...], "features":[...], "rating":0}"""</span>

<span class="va">response</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="va">client</span>.<span class="fn">chat</span>.<span class="fn">completions</span>.<span class="fn">create</span>(
    <span class="va">model</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="st">"gpt-4"</span>,
    <span class="va">messages</span><span class="op">=</span>[
        {<span class="st">"role"</span>: <span class="st">"system"</span>, <span class="st">"content"</span>: <span class="st">"You are a JSON extraction tool. Return ONLY valid JSON, no explanations or markdown formatting."</span>},
        {<span class="st">"role"</span>: <span class="st">"user"</span>, <span class="st">"content"</span>: <span class="va">prompt</span>}
    ],
    <span class="va">temperature</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="nm">0</span>
)

<span class="cm"># Parse and use the structured response</span>
<span class="va">content</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="va">response</span>.<span class="fn">choices</span>[<span class="nm">0</span>].<span class="fn">message</span>.<span class="fn">content</span>
<span class="va">data</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">json</span>.<span class="fn">loads</span>(<span class="va">content</span>)
<span class="fn">print</span>(<span class="st">f"Product: {data['name']} at ${data['price']}"</span>)
<span class="fn">print</span>(<span class="st">f"Rating: {data['rating']}/5"</span>)</code></pre>

<div class="key-concept"><strong>Key Concept:</strong> Lower temperature (closer to 0) produces more consistent outputs. For structured data extraction, always use temperature=0 to minimize randomness.</div>

<section class="section" id="schema-design"><span class="section-label">Schema-Based Approaches</span><h2>JSON Schema and Structured Extraction</h2><p>For complex nested data, define a JSON schema upfront. This makes expectations crystal clear and helps the model understand exactly what structure to produce. You can even include constraints like enum values, min/max ranges, and required fields.</p>

<div class="code-header"><span class="code-lang">Python</span><button class="copy-btn">Copy</button></div><pre><code><span class="cm"># Define a detailed JSON schema for structured extraction</span>
<span class="va">schema</span> <span class="op">=</span> {
    <span class="st">"type"</span>: <span class="st">"object"</span>,
    <span class="st">"properties"</span>: {
        <span class="st">"sentiment"</span>: {
            <span class="st">"type"</span>: <span class="st">"string</span>,
            <span class="st">"enum"</span>: [<span class="st">"positive"</span>, <span class="st">"negative"</span>, <span class="st">"neutral"</span>, <span class="st">"mixed"</span>],
            <span class="st">"description"</span>: <span class="st">"Overall sentiment of the review"</span>
        },
        <span class="st">"score"</span>: {
            <span class="st">"type"</span>: <span class="st">"number"</span>,
            <span class="st">"minimum"</span>: <span class="nm">0</span>,
            <span class="st">"maximum"</span>: <span class="nm">1</span>,
            <span class="st">"description"</span>: <span class="st">"Confidence score 0-1"</span>
        },
        <span class="st">"key_aspects"</span>: {
            <span class="st">"type"</span>: <span class="st">"array"</span>,
            <span class="st">"items"</span>: {
                <span class="st">"type"</span>: <span class="st">"object"</span>,
                <span class="st">"properties"</span>: {
                    <span class="st">"aspect"</span>: {<span class="st">"type"</span>: <span class="st">"string"</span>},
                    <span class="st">"opinion"</span>: {<span class="st">"type"</span>: <span class="st">"string"</span>},
                    <span class="st">"aspect_sentiment"</span>: {<span class="st">"type"</span>: <span class="st">"string"</span>, <span class="st">"enum"</span>: [<span class="st">"positive"</span>, <span class="st">"negative"</span>, <span class="st">"neutral"</span>]}
                },
                <span class="st">"required"</span>: [<span class="st">"aspect"</span>, <span class="st">"aspect_sentiment"</span>]
            },
            <span class="st">"minItems"</span>: <span class="nm">1</span>,
            <span class="st">"maxItems"</span>: <span class="nm">5</span>
        },
        <span class="st">"explanation"</span>: {<span class="st">"type"</span>: <span class="st">"string"</span>}
    },
    <span class="st">"required"</span>: [<span class="st">"sentiment"</span>, <span class="st">"score"</span>, <span class="st">"key_aspects"</span>]
}

<span class="va">review_text</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="st">"""Excellent product! The noise cancellation is incredible and battery life lasts all day.
Only downside is the price, but quality justifies the cost. Highly recommend."""</span>

<span class="va">prompt</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="st">f"""Analyze this review and return JSON matching this schema:
{json.dumps(schema, indent=2)}

Review: {review_text}

Return ONLY the JSON object, nothing else."""</span>

<span class="va">response</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="va">client</span>.<span class="fn">chat</span>.<span class="fn">completions</span>.<span class="fn">create</span>(
    <span class="va">model</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="st">"gpt-4"</span>,
    <span class="va">messages</span><span class="op">=</span>[{<span class="st">"role"</span>: <span class="st">"user"</span>, <span class="st">"content"</span>: <span class="va">prompt</span>}],
    <span class="va">temperature</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="nm">0</span>
)

<span class="va">result</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">json</span>.<span class="fn">loads</span>(<span class="va">response</span>.<span class="fn">choices</span>[<span class="nm">0</span>].<span class="fn">message</span>.<span class="fn">content</span>)
<span class="kw">for</span> <span class="va">aspect</span> <span class="kw">in</span> <span class="va">result</span>[<span class="st">'key_aspects'</span>]:
    <span class="fn">print</span>(<span class="st">f"{aspect['aspect']}: {aspect['aspect_sentiment']}"</span>)</code></pre>

<div class="callout-box tip"><strong>Pro Tip:</strong> Include descriptions in your schema. The more context the model has about what each field means, the better the extraction quality.</div>

<section class="section" id="parsing-extraction"><span class="section-label">Data Extraction Patterns</span><h2>Extracting Lists, Tables, and Nested Data</h2><p>Use JSON arrays for extracting multiple items. This is more reliable than markdown tables for programmatic processing, especially when dealing with nested or complex data structures.</p>

<div class="code-header"><span class="code-lang">Python</span><button class="copy-btn">Copy</button></div><pre><code><span class="cm"># Extract multiple items as JSON array</span>
<span class="va">prompt</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="st">"""Identify the top 5 programming languages for AI/ML development.
Return as JSON array where each item has:
- name (string)
- year_created (integer)
- primary_use (string, one of: 'data-science', 'backend', 'systems', 'web', 'scripting')
- adoption_level (integer 1-10)
- key_library (string, main library used in AI/ML)

Return ONLY valid JSON array, no other text."""</span>

<span class="va">response</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="va">client</span>.<span class="fn">chat</span>.<span class="fn">completions</span>.<span class="fn">create</span>(
    <span class="va">model</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="st">"gpt-4"</span>,
    <span class="va">messages</span><span class="op">=</span>[{<span class="st">"role"</span>: <span class="st">"user"</span>, <span class="st">"content"</span>: <span class="va">prompt</span>}],
    <span class="va">temperature</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="nm">0</span>
)

<span class="va">languages</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">json</span>.<span class="fn">loads</span>(<span class="va">response</span>.<span class="fn">choices</span>[<span class="nm">0</span>].<span class="fn">message</span>.<span class="fn">content</span>)

<span class="cm"># Process structured data programmatically</span>
<span class="kw">for</span> <span class="va">lang</span> <span class="kw">in</span> <span class="va">languages</span>:
    <span class="fn">print</span>(<span class="st">f"{lang['name']} ({lang['year_created']})"</span>)
    <span class="fn">print</span>(<span class="st">f"  Adoption: {lang['adoption_level']}/10"</span>)
    <span class="fn">print</span>(<span class="st">f"  Key Library: {lang['key_library']}"</span>)</code></pre>

<div class="compare-grid"><div class="compare-item"><div class="compare-title">JSON Array</div><div class="compare-content">Machine-readable, easy iteration, supports nesting.</div></div><div class="compare-item"><div class="compare-title">Markdown Table</div><div class="compare-content">Human-readable, harder to parse programmatically.</div></div><div class="compare-item"><div class="compare-title">CSV Format</div><div class="compare-content">Simple 2D tables, limited for complex nested data.</div></div></div>

<section class="section" id="error-handling"><span class="section-label">Robustness &amp; Production Reliability</span><h2>Validation and Error Handling</h2><p>LLMs sometimes produce malformed JSON, extra text, or violate schema constraints. Production systems need defensive code to handle failures gracefully. Build retry logic, fallback strategies, and detailed validation.</p>

<div class="code-header"><span class="code-lang">Python</span><button class="copy-btn">Copy</button></div><pre><code><span class="kw">import</span> <span class="im">re</span>
<span class="kw">import</span> <span class="im">json</span>

<span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">safe_json_parse</span>(<span class="va">response_text</span>):
    <span class="st">"""Attempt to parse JSON with multiple fallback strategies."""</span>

    <span class="cm"># Strategy 1: Try direct parse</span>
    <span class="kw">try</span>:
        <span class="kw">return</span> <span class="fn">json</span>.<span class="fn">loads</span>(<span class="va">response_text</span>)
    <span class="kw">except</span> <span class="fn">json</span>.<span class="fn">JSONDecodeError</span>:
        <span class="kw">pass</span>

    <span class="cm"># Strategy 2: Extract JSON substring (model wraps in markdown or extra text)</span>
    <span class="va">json_match</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">re</span>.<span class="fn">search</span>(<span class="st">r'(\{.*\}|\[.*\])'</span>, <span class="va">response_text</span>, <span class="fn">re</span>.<span class="fn">DOTALL</span>)
    <span class="kw">if</span> <span class="va">json_match</span>:
        <span class="kw">try</span>:
            <span class="kw">return</span> <span class="fn">json</span>.<span class="fn">loads</span>(<span class="va">json_match</span>.<span class="fn">group</span>(<span class="nm">1</span>))
        <span class="kw">except</span>:
            <span class="kw">pass</span>

    <span class="cm"># Strategy 3: Return error structure</span>
    <span class="kw">return</span> {<span class="st">"error"</span>: <span class="st">"Failed to parse JSON"</span>, <span class="st">"raw"</span>: <span class="va">response_text</span>}

<span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">validate_response</span>(<span class="va">data</span>, <span class="va">required_keys</span>):
    <span class="st">"""Validate response has required keys and no errors."""</span>
    <span class="kw">if</span> <span class="st">"error"</span> <span class="kw">in</span> <span class="va">data</span>:
        <span class="kw">raise</span> <span class="fn">ValueError</span>(<span class="st">f"Parsing error: {data['error']}"</span>)

    <span class="va">missing</span> <span class="op">=</span> [<span class="va">k</span> <span class="kw">for</span> <span class="va">k</span> <span class="kw">in</span> <span class="va">required_keys</span> <span class="kw">if</span> <span class="va">k</span> <span class="kw">not</span> <span class="kw">in</span> <span class="va">data</span>]
    <span class="kw">if</span> <span class="va">missing</span>:
        <span class="kw">raise</span> <span class="fn">ValueError</span>(<span class="st">f"Missing required keys: {missing}"</span>)
    <span class="kw">return</span> <span class="kw">True</span>

<span class="cm"># Usage with error handling</span>
<span class="kw">try</span>:
    <span class="va">data</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">safe_json_parse</span>(<span class="va">response</span>.<span class="fn">choices</span>[<span class="nm">0</span>].<span class="fn">message</span>.<span class="fn">content</span>)
    <span class="fn">validate_response</span>(<span class="va">data</span>, [<span class="st">'sentiment'</span>, <span class="st">'score'</span>])
    <span class="fn">print</span>(<span class="st">"Valid response received"</span>)
<span class="kw">except</span> <span class="fn">ValueError</span> <span class="kw">as</span> <span class="va">e</span>:
    <span class="fn">print</span>(<span class="st">f"Validation failed: {e}"</span>)</code></pre>

<section class="section" id="production"><span class="section-label">Production Systems</span><h2>Building Robust Data Extraction Pipelines</h2><p>Combine all techniques into a complete, production-ready pipeline with logging, retry logic, and database integration.</p>

<div class="code-header"><span class="code-lang">Python</span><button class="copy-btn">Copy</button></div><pre><code><span class="kw">class</span> <span class="fn">StructuredExtractor</span>:
    <span class="st">"""Production-grade structured data extraction using LLM."""</span>

    <span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">__init__</span>(<span class="va">self</span>, <span class="va">schema</span>, <span class="va">max_retries</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="nm">3</span>):
        <span class="va">self</span>.<span class="va">client</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">OpenAI</span>()
        <span class="va">self</span>.<span class="va">schema</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="va">schema</span>
        <span class="va">self</span>.<span class="va">max_retries</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="va">max_retries</span>

    <span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">extract</span>(<span class="va">self</span>, <span class="va">text</span>, <span class="va">system_prompt</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="kw">None</span>):
        <span class="st">"""Extract structured data from text with retry logic."""</span>
        <span class="va">system_prompt</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="va">system_prompt</span> <span class="op">or</span> <span class="st">"Extract and return ONLY valid JSON."</span>

        <span class="kw">for</span> <span class="va">attempt</span> <span class="kw">in</span> <span class="fn">range</span>(<span class="va">self</span>.<span class="va">max_retries</span>):
            <span class="kw">try</span>:
                <span class="va">prompt</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="st">f"""Extract data and return JSON:
Schema: {json.dumps(self.schema)}
Text: {text}"""</span>

                <span class="va">response</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="va">self</span>.<span class="va">client</span>.<span class="fn">chat</span>.<span class="fn">completions</span>.<span class="fn">create</span>(
                    <span class="va">model</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="st">"gpt-4"</span>,
                    <span class="va">messages</span><span class="op">=</span>[
                        {<span class="st">"role"</span>: <span class="st">"system"</span>, <span class="st">"content"</span>: <span class="va">system_prompt</span>},
                        {<span class="st">"role"</span>: <span class="st">"user"</span>, <span class="st">"content"</span>: <span class="va">prompt</span>}
                    ],
                    <span class="va">temperature</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="nm">0</span>
                )

                <span class="va">data</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">safe_json_parse</span>(<span class="va">response</span>.<span class="fn">choices</span>[<span class="nm">0</span>].<span class="fn">message</span>.<span class="fn">content</span>)
                <span class="fn">validate_response</span>(<span class="va">data</span>, <span class="va">self</span>.<span class="va">schema</span>.<span class="fn">get</span>(<span class="st">'required'</span>, []))
                <span class="kw">return</span> <span class="va">data</span>

            <span class="kw">except</span> <span class="fn">Exception</span> <span class="kw">as</span> <span class="va">e</span>:
                <span class="kw">if</span> <span class="va">attempt</span> <span class="op">==</span> <span class="va">self</span>.<span class="va">max_retries</span> <span class="op">-</span> <span class="nm">1</span>:
                    <span class="kw">raise</span> <span class="fn">Exception</span>(<span class="st">f"Extraction failed after {self.max_retries} attempts: {str(e)}"</span>)

<span class="cm"># Usage</span>
<span class="va">extractor</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">StructuredExtractor</span>(<span class="va">schema</span>)
<span class="va">result</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="va">extractor</span>.<span class="fn">extract</span>(<span class="va">text</span>)</code></pre>

<div class="callout-box success"><strong>Best Practice:</strong> Always test your extraction pipeline with diverse inputs before deploying to production. Build a test suite with expected edge cases.</div>

<section class="section" id="exercises"><span class="section-label">Practice</span><h2>Hands-On Exercises</h2><ol><li><strong>JSON Extraction:</strong> Create a prompt that extracts customer information (name, email, phone, company) as JSON from unstructured business card text.</li><li><strong>Schema Design:</strong> Design a schema for extracting meeting notes with attendees, action items, decisions, and next steps. Use nested objects for action items (person, task, deadline).</li><li><strong>Error Handling:</strong> Write code that extracts JSON from 10 different review texts and handles parsing failures gracefully. Log failures for debugging.</li><li><strong>Batch Processing:</strong> Create a function that extracts data from a batch of texts and saves results to a JSON file with error tracking.</li></ol></section>

<section class="section" id="summary"><span class="section-label">Summary</span><h2>Key Takeaways</h2><ul><li><strong>JSON Output:</strong> Request JSON explicitly and use temperature=0 for consistency. Always include clear examples of the format you want.</li><li><strong>Schema Definition:</strong> Define detailed JSON schemas with type constraints, enums, and required fields. The more explicit, the better the extraction.</li><li><strong>Extraction Patterns:</strong> Use JSON arrays for lists, nested objects for complex data. These are more reliable than markdown for programmatic processing.</li><li><strong>Error Handling:</strong> Implement multiple parsing strategies (direct parse, substring extraction, error logging). Never assume responses are well-formed.</li><li><strong>Validation:</strong> Check for required keys, correct types, and value ranges after parsing. This prevents silent failures downstream.</li><li><strong>Production Readiness:</strong> Add retry logic, comprehensive logging, and test suites before deploying extraction pipelines to production.</li></ul></div>

